SUMMARY:Contemplative Citizenship
DESCRIPTION:Contemplative Citizenship:\nLord\, make me an instrument of your peace.\nOctober 13 – November 10\n7 – 8:00 PM in the Chapel\nIn person and via Zoom \nThis Fall\, our worship and teaching will be guided by a single line from the Prayer of Saint Francis: “Lord\, make me an instrument of your peace.” We will begin this initiative at our Saturday Night Mass on October 3\, with local musician and pastor Liz Fulmer leading music that inspires us to embody God’s peace in our lives. \nOn Tuesday\, October 13\, we will start a 5-week Fall Contemplative Citizenship series in which we will reflect on various lines from the prayer\, exploring what it means to embody this prayer in both our personal lives and in our civic responsibilities\, especially during this election season when our country feels divided and stressed.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/contemplative-citizenship/2026-10-20/
LOCATION:Saint James Chapel and Zoom\, PA\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Featured-image-CC-2.jpg
GEO:41.2033216;-77.1945247
END:VEVENT
